---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms | Ops Error Atlas"
	description="Read the usage terms and limitations for Ops Error Atlas technical troubleshooting content."
>
	<section class="page-hero section-inner">
		<h1 class="page-title">Terms</h1>
		<p class="page-intro">
			Ops Error Atlas provides educational troubleshooting references for backend and network
			errors. Use the guidance carefully and verify commands in your own environment.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="section section-inner">
		<div class="text-panel rich-copy">
			<h2>Educational use</h2>
			<p>
				The guides and Error Explainer are written for general technical education and
				operational reference. They are not a substitute for incident response procedures,
				vendor support, or environment-specific review by a qualified engineer.
			</p>

			<h2>No production guarantee</h2>
			<p>
				Command examples can behave differently across Linux distributions, containers, cloud
				providers, proxies, and application runtimes. Always inspect commands before running
				them, especially on production systems.
			</p>

			<h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
			<p>
				Ops Error Atlas aims to keep explanations practical and accurate, but backend and
				network software changes over time. Content may be updated when better diagnosis
				steps, clearer examples, or missing failure modes are identified.
			</p>

			<h2>External links</h2>
			<p>
				Some pages may link to documentation, tools, or third-party resources. External sites
				have their own terms and privacy policies. Ops Error Atlas is not responsible for
				their content or availability.
			</p>

			<h2>Advertising</h2>
			<p>
				The site may display advertising after approval from an advertising provider. Ads, if
				enabled, help support the maintenance of free troubleshooting content.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				If you find an error, outdated command, or unsafe recommendation, please use the
				contact page to report it so the guide can be reviewed.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
